# Dot Wars — development rules

## Architecture

TypeScript monorepo. Shared types, interfaces, and DTOs live in `packages/shared`.

## Server (Authoritative Server)

All game logic, troop updates, collisions, unit movement, and winner checks happen ONLY on the server (NestJS + Colyseus). The client receives state deltas (State Sync).

## Client

The battlefield is rendered with PixiJS v8 inside a React canvas component. All UI (buttons, badges, timers) is React + Tailwind CSS on top of the canvas.

Menu dock is always three pills via `OrigamiDock` (same width `max-w-80`, same gaps). Slot 1 = Vs bots, slot 2 = public matchmaking (currently a disabled Coming soon stub), slot 3 = Invite to PvP. On the public search screen, Cancel must sit in slot 2. Do not add or remove dock slots without keeping that alignment.

## Security

Player auth is via Gram/TON wallet: the server verifies `ton_proof` and issues a session bound to the wallet address. Nickname and stats belong to the wallet.
